# MeterNet hotspot rules for macOS. hotspot.sh loads them into the pf anchor
# com.apple/meternet, which macOS's own /etc/pf.conf already evaluates
# (rdr-anchor and anchor "com.apple/*"); no system file is edited.
#
# Internet Sharing provides the Wi-Fi access point on bridge100, DHCP, DNS
# and NAT. These rules decide which phones may go further:
# - everyone may reach the box itself: DHCP, DNS, the portal on 443 (which
#   also proxies the CKB testnet RPC) and the Fiber node's wss on 8443.
#   <walled> is empty unless WALLED_HOSTS adds hosts; it is not used for the
#   CKB RPC because that host shares Cloudflare addresses with other sites;
# - phones in <paid> may reach anything, and pf counts their bytes per
#   address (meterd reads them with `pfctl -vT show`);
# - everyone else is blocked. Plain-HTTP requests from unpaid phones, such
#   as the OS captive-portal checks, are redirected to the box's portal.
#
# hotspot.sh passes the interface and the box address as macros.

table <paid> persist
table <walled> persist

rdr pass on $iface proto tcp from ! <paid> to ! $box port 80 -> $box port 8080

pass in quick on $iface proto udp from any port 68 to any port 67
pass in quick on $iface proto { tcp udp } from any to $box keep state
pass in quick on $iface proto tcp from any to <walled> port 443 keep state
pass in quick on $iface from <paid> to any keep state
block drop in quick on $iface all
